  "rows": [
    {
      "number": 18862,
      "text": "[FALSO] Although it shows two humps, the sign indicates an uneven or damaged road, not a series of hill crests."
    },
    {
      "number": 18865,
      "text": "[FALSO] The hill crest sign shows a single hump; the two humps shown here indicate an uneven road."
    },
    {
      "number": 18866,
      "text": "[FALSO] A dip and a hill crest each have their own sign; the two humps shown indicate an uneven road."
    },
    {
      "number": 18879,
      "text": "[VERO] The sign, which shows a single hump, is the warning sign for a hill crest."
    },
    {
      "number": 18914,
      "text": "[FALSO] The hill crest sign shows an upward hump; the downward dip shown here indicates a dip in the road."
    },
    {
      "number": 20858,
      "text": "[VERO] Since a one-way road has no oncoming traffic, overtaking is permitted near or at hill crests, where it would be prohibited on two-way roads."
    },
    {
      "number": 20910,
      "text": "[FALSO] A one-way road has only one direction of travel, so there are not two directions to separate; the line divides lanes travelling in the same direction and has no connection to hill crests."
